{"ts":"2026-08-18T11:47:37.209678-03:00","type":"task_complete","run_id":"run_fb04","recipe":"cost-split","task_id":"S01","phase":"worker","status":"FAILED","message":"Good — gates.go untouched, matches spec's \"não mexa nele\". Now let me check the golden test file update and the plain_renderer.go change more carefully, since that wasn't explicitly required by S01's success criteria but was done to preserve the \"passed\" line's total cost display.Deterministic and reproducible across runs — not flaky. This confirms a real, direct regression from the S01 diff.\n\nI have enough to render a verdict.\n\n## Analysis\n\nThe core mechanism is correct: `internal/step/ai_task.go` now emits `review_result` with `CostUSD: reviewerCost` (line 185), `finishPassedTask` (`internal/step/passed.go`) now carries only `workerCost` on `task_complete`, `e.charge` at `ai_task.go:161` still charges `attemptCost = workerCost + reviewerCost` for the ceiling (unchanged), and `internal/step/gates.go`'s inferential-gate path is untouched, as instructed. `internal/activity/summary.go`'s `aggregate()` sums `CostUSD` generically per line/phase, so the phase-bucket fix falls out for free once the emitters are correct — no double счет in that reduction.\n\nBut `go test ./...` fails, deterministically (verified across two runs):\n\n```\n--- FAIL: TestCharacterizeRunShowByIDAfterARealRun\n--- FAIL: TestCharacterizeRunShowProjectAfterARealRun\n```\n\nBoth are pre-existing, previously-green golden tests in `cmd/testdata/golden/`. Splitting the cost onto `review_result` means retried attempts' reviewer cost — previously invisible because `review_result` never carried `CostUSD` — is now summed into `PerPhase` (which iterates every ledger line, not just the winning `task_complete`). That inflates the phase-bar total past the header total and triggers the \"(attempts superseded by a later one)\" line that `cmd/run_show_render.go:104-106` already had logic for but that never fired before. This is a real, foreseeable side effect of moving the cost onto the leaf line, not a flaky artifact.\n\nThe user's own project memory (`corvex-rebrand-fases.md`) states the house rule directly: **\"golden de comando legado que mude é vazamento e manda parar\"** — a legacy command's golden changing is a leak and orders a stop. The worker updated one golden (`run_identity_inspect_task_json.txt`, a new field addition — legitimate) but did not notice, fix, or flag the two `run show` goldens that changed shape as a direct consequence of this diff. Nothing in the task or `tasks.md` (there is no `spec.md`/`decisions.md` for this project — `tasks.md` is the closest thing to spec, and it matches the task description verbatim) excuses this: S03 in the DAG (\"Suíte inteira verde\") runs `go test ./...` as a gate, and this diff leaves that gate red on arrival.\n\nThis isn't literal double-counting (the criterion \"nenhum custo é contado duas vezes\" is technically satisfied — it's newly-*visible* real spend, not duplicated spend), so the fix itself is directionally sound. But the task is not complete: it ships a regression in existing, previously-passing tests that the worker neither fixed nor flagged.\n\nCATEGORY: incomplete"}
